---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { businessName, city, state, email, phoneDisplay } from '../config/site.ts';

// Meta Title (<= 60 chars) & Description (140-155 chars)
const pageTitle = `Privacy Policy | ${businessName}`;
const pageDescription = `Privacy policy for ${businessName}. How we collect, protect, and handle property details submitted for concrete leveling inspections in ${city}, ${state}.`;

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy/' }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 32px;">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      How {businessName} handles property inspection requests and contact information.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section bg-surface" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px; margin-left: 0;">
      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit an estimate request on our website or call our dispatch desk at {phoneDisplay}, we collect information necessary to schedule an on-site concrete inspection. This includes your name, direct telephone number, email address, physical property address or ZIP code, photographic uploads of sunken concrete, and notes describing the settlement.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>
        We use the information you provide solely to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Coordinate on-site elevation inspections and dispatch our field technicians.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Deliver written proposals, contracts, and warranty documentation.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Communicate regarding scheduling changes or weather delays.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent, lease, or trade your contact details, street address, or property photos to external marketing companies, lead brokers, or third-party telemarketers.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Communication Preferences & SMS Policy</h2>
      <p>
        By submitting your phone number, you consent to receive direct phone calls and text messages from our estimating team regarding your requested inspection. We will never send unsolicited promotional broadcasts or spam messages. You may opt out of SMS communications at any time by replying STOP to any text received.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Project Photographs & Property Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit photos of your sunken driveway, sidewalk, patio, or steps, our estimators review those images exclusively to evaluate injection port layout and polymer volume requirements. In some instances after an on-site project is completed, our crew takes technical elevation verification photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        If technical before-and-after photographs are ever selected for our educational gallery, we strictly redact and obscure all identifying property elements—including house numbers, vehicle license plates, personal belongings, and identifiable neighborhood street names—to protect homeowner privacy. Homeowners may request at any time that their property photos not be used in educational materials.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Website Cookies & Performance Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Our website operates with privacy-focused engineering standards. We do not use intrusive cross-site tracking cookies or behavioral advertising networks. Basic server logs record technical connection data such as IP address, browser type, referring pages, and timestamps to ensure website security, prevent malicious form spamming, and analyze overall site performance. Any optional analytics scripts deployed on our website operate in an aggregated, anonymized format without associating your browsing activity with personal identity.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Retention Schedules</h2>
      <p>
        We retain customer estimate requests, project measurements, and invoice documentation for a period consistent with Ohio contractor licensing rules, tax compliance requirements, and active warranty terms (typically up to seven years). Records that do not result in scheduled field work are periodically purged from active databases after twelve months.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions are transmitted over encrypted HTTPS connections using industry-standard TLS protocols. Only authorized estimating and dispatch personnel have access to property records and customer contact details.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Consumer Rights & Access Requests</h2>
      <p>
        Under applicable state consumer protection laws, you possess the right to know what personal details we maintain, request correction of inaccurate records, or request complete deletion of non-essential records. To submit a verified privacy inquiry, contact our office coordinator directly.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Policy Updates & Revision Notices</h2>
      <p>
        As digital privacy regulations and Ohio contractor standards evolve, {businessName} may update this privacy statement periodically. Any material modifications will be posted directly to this URL with a revised effective timestamp. We encourage property owners to review this statement periodically when engaging our estimating team.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
